  D("o",{etymology:E("The English letter name descends through Latin and Greek omicron from Phoenician ʿayin ‘eye’; Greek adapted the sign as a vowel letter.",null,"Phoenician ʿayin > Greek omicron",null,"Etymonline, O (https://www.etymonline.com/word/O)."),contexts:[C("o.s1","语法","The word “orange” begins with the letter O, followed by r.","“Orange”這個詞以字母 O 開頭，後面接 r。","O names a written alphabet letter, not the sound alone.","The quoted word is the subject; begins with takes the preposition with.","The sentence explicitly identifies the first written letter in a spelling.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The student wrote that the word ocean starts with P.","The student wrote that the word ocean starts with O.","Ocean begins with O, not P; the mistake confuses the target letter with another alphabet position.")],quiz:[Q("o.q1","o.s1","meaning","Which word starts with the letter O?",["ocean","cabin","maple"],"ocean","Ocean begins with the fifteenth English alphabet letter, O.","meaning"),Q("o.q2","o.s1","alphabet","What letter comes immediately after N?",["O","M","P"],"O","O follows N in the English alphabet.","meaning"),Q("o.q3","o.s1","context","In “She circled O on the answer sheet,” what does O identify?",["an alphabet letter choice","a musical instrument","a unit of distance"],"an alphabet letter choice","The answer sheet presents O as a written character.","context"),Q("o.q4","o.s1","etymology","The letter O ultimately traces through Greek to a Phoenician sign associated with ___.",["an eye","a ship","a mountain"],"an eye","The ancestor was Phoenician ʿayin, whose name meant ‘eye’.","meaning")]});
