  D("oasis",{etymology:E("English came through Latin and Greek oasis; Greek may have borrowed it from an Egyptian/Coptic term for a fertile place, but the remote source is uncertain.",null,"Greek oasis; earlier source uncertain",null,"Etymonline, oasis (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oasis)."),contexts:[C("oasis.s1","地理","A spring-fed oasis let the travelers refill their water skins before crossing the dunes.","泉水滋養的綠洲讓旅人能在穿越沙丘前裝滿水囊。","Oasis names a fertile place with water amid a desert.","A follows the article; let + object + bare infinitive expresses permission or ability.","The spring and desert setting establish the literal geographical sense."),C("oasis.s2","比喻","The quiet reading room was an oasis of calm during the noisy renovation.","施工期間，安靜的閱覽室成了喧鬧中的一方寧靜天地。","Oasis is metaphorical: a pleasant refuge within a difficult or unpleasant setting.","An oasis of + abstract noun specifies the quality; during gives the surrounding situation.","The room is not in a desert; it provides welcome calm amid disruption.")],mistakes:[M("number","A line of palm trees and a well made the travelers call the place an oasises.","A line of palm trees and a well made the travelers call the place an oasis.","Oasis is singular; its plural is oases, not oasises.")],quiz:[Q("oasis.q1","oasis.s1","meaning","In a desert, an oasis usually provides ___.",["water and vegetation","a glacier and sea ice","a paved airport"],"water and vegetation","A desert oasis is a fertile place where water allows plants to grow.","meaning"),Q("oasis.q2","oasis.s2","meaning","Calling a quiet garden an oasis in a busy city emphasizes that it is ___.",["a pleasant refuge","a dry salt flat","a crowded traffic lane"],"a pleasant refuge","The figurative sense is a calm or pleasant place amid difficulty.","meaning"),Q("oasis.q3","oasis.s1","plural","What is the standard plural of oasis?",["oases","oasises","oasies"],"oases","Oasis forms its plural by changing -is to -es.","plural"),Q("oasis.q4","oasis.s2","context","Which use is metaphorical?",["The courtyard felt like an oasis of shade in the hot city.","The map marks an oasis beside the desert track.","The well supplied the oasis with water."],"The courtyard felt like an oasis of shade in the hot city.","A city courtyard is compared to a desert refuge to convey relief.","context")]});
  D("oat",{etymology:E("Old English āte, from a Germanic word for the grain; its further origin is uncertain.",null,"Old English āte",null,"Etymonline, oat (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oat)."),contexts:[C("oat.s1","农业","The oat is a cereal crop grown in the north field and harvested in late summer.","農夫在北邊田地種植燕麥作物，並在夏末收割穀粒。","Oat names the cereal crop and its edible grain.","The singular count noun oat names the crop; its grain is harvested for food and feed.","The field and harvest indicate the plant/grain sense rather than a prepared dish.")],mistakes:[M("word-choice","The farmer planted oat berries across both fields and sold the crop by the sack.","The farmer planted oat grains across both fields and sold the crop by the sack.","Oats are cereal grains, not berries; the crop is planted as seeds or grains.")],quiz:[Q("oat.q1","oat.s1","meaning","Oats are commonly grown for ___.",["food and animal feed","making glass","producing table salt"],"food and animal feed","The grain is used for human food and animal feed.","meaning"),Q("oat.q2","oat.s1","context","Which sentence refers to the crop in a field?",["Oats ripened under the late-summer sun.","She stirred oatmeal into the bowl.","The horse ate an oatcake."],"Oats ripened under the late-summer sun.","Ripening under the sun describes the cereal crop growing in the field.","context"),Q("oat.q3","oat.s1","plural","Choose the usual crop form: “They grow ____ for porridge.”",["oats","oat's","oaties"],"oats","Oats is the customary plural form for the crop and its grains.","plural"),Q("oat.q4","oat.s1","meaning","Which item comes from the oat plant?",["a grain used in porridge","a cocoa bean","a potato tuber"],"a grain used in porridge","Oat grains are milled or cooked for foods such as porridge.","meaning")]});
  D("oath",{etymology:E("Old English āþ, from Proto-Germanic *aiþaz; the word developed from a solemn pledge to include a curse or profane exclamation.",null,"Proto-Germanic *aiþaz",null,"Etymonline, oath (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oath)."),contexts:[C("oath.s1","法律","Before testifying, the witness took an oath to tell the truth.","作證前，證人宣誓要說實話。","Oath is a solemn promise made before giving evidence.","Took an oath is a common verb-noun collocation; to introduces the pledged action.","The court setting and promise to tell the truth select the pledge sense."),C("oath.s2","语言","“Damn!” was the oath he muttered when the jar slipped from his hand.","罐子從手中滑落時，他低聲罵了一句「該死！」","Oath means a swear word or curse in this use.","The quoted exclamation is followed by a relative clause identifying its speaker.","The angry interjection is a curse, not a promise made under oath.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The witness took an oath to keep silent, then truthfully answered every question.","The witness took an oath to tell the truth, then answered every question.","An oath to keep silent conflicts with answering; use a pledge consistent with the later action.")],quiz:[Q("oath.q1","oath.s1","meaning","A witness under oath has made ___.",["a solemn promise","a casual guess","a weather forecast"],"a solemn promise","In legal settings, an oath is a solemn pledge to speak truthfully.","meaning"),Q("oath.q2","oath.s2","meaning","In “He swore an oath at the broken machine,” oath can mean ___.",["an angry curse","a legal witness statement","a wedding promise"],"an angry curse","The verb swore and broken machine suggest a profane exclamation.","meaning"),Q("oath.q3","oath.s1","context","Which situation calls for the pledge sense?",["A witness promises to give truthful testimony.","A cook mutters a curse after burning a hand.","A sailor names a new boat."],"A witness promises to give truthful testimony.","A courtroom promise to tell the truth is the pledge sense.","context"),Q("oath.q4","oath.s2","context","Which sentence uses oath as a curse?",["He let out an oath when the hammer struck his thumb.","She took an oath before the judge.","The officer administered the oath of office."],"He let out an oath when the hammer struck his thumb.","The painful accident prompts a swear word, unlike formal pledges in the other sentences.","context")]});
  D("oatmeal",{etymology:E("A compound of oat and meal; meal comes from Old English melu ‘ground grain’ and is related to mill.",null,"oat + meal (< Old English melu)",null,"Etymonline, meal (https://www.etymonline.com/word/meal); Etymonline, oat (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oat)."),contexts:[C("oatmeal.s1","饮食","She simmered oatmeal with milk until it thickened into a warm porridge.","她用牛奶慢煮燕麥片，直到變成濃稠的熱粥。","Oatmeal refers to oats prepared as a meal or porridge.","Uncountable food noun as the object of simmered; until introduces the result.","The cooking process and porridge texture indicate prepared food, not the crop in a field.")],mistakes:[M("spelling","The cook sprinkled oatmel with cinnamon.","The cook sprinkled oatmeal with cinnamon.","Oatmeal is spelled with the second a; oatmel is a misspelling.")],quiz:[Q("oatmeal.q1","oatmeal.s1","meaning","A bowl of oatmeal is usually made from ___.",["cooked oats","ground coffee beans","mashed olives"],"cooked oats","Oatmeal is oats prepared as food, often porridge.","meaning"),Q("oatmeal.q2","oatmeal.s1","context","Which sentence uses oatmeal as a prepared dish?",["The child ate oatmeal with sliced banana.","Oats were growing in the field.","The mill stored grain for next year."],"The child ate oatmeal with sliced banana.","Eating it with fruit identifies the cooked breakfast food.","context"),Q("oatmeal.q3","oatmeal.s1","countability","Choose the natural way to order two servings.",["two bowls of oatmeal","two bowls of oatmeals","two bowl of oatmeal"],"two bowls of oatmeal","A bowl is the count unit; oatmeal itself is ordinarily uncountable.","countability"),Q("oatmeal.q4","oatmeal.s1","word-choice","For a warm breakfast made from oats, order ____. ",["oatmeal","oakmeal","oatiness"],"oatmeal","Oatmeal names oats cooked or prepared as food.","word-choice")]});
  D("oats",{etymology:E("Oats is the conventional plural form of oat, from Old English āte; the crop is often named in the plural in modern English.",null,"Old English āte",null,"Etymonline, oat (https://www.etymonline.com/word/oat)."),contexts:[C("oats.s1","农业","Oats provide both breakfast grain for people and feed for the stable horses.","燕麥既可作人的早餐穀物，也可作馬廄裡馬匹的飼料。","Oats names the cereal crop as a food and feed grain.","Plural-form noun is the subject and takes provide; both…and pairs uses.","The two uses listed—human food and animal feed—match the crop sense.")],mistakes:[M("spelling","The farm grows oatss for porridge and horse feed.","The farm grows oats for porridge and horse feed.","Oats is spelled with one s at the end; oatss adds an extra letter.")],quiz:[Q("oats.q1","oats.s1","meaning","Which pair are common uses for oats?",["porridge and animal feed","glass and cement","dye and fuel only"],"porridge and animal feed","Oats are a cereal crop eaten by people and used as livestock feed.","meaning"),Q("oats.q2","oats.s1","context","Which sentence refers to oats as a crop?",["The farmer cut the oats before the rain.","She ate a bowl of oatmeal.","He stirred a spoonful of honey."],"The farmer cut the oats before the rain.","Cutting a field crop before rain describes harvesting oats.","context"),Q("oats.q3","oats.s1","plural","Complete the sentence: “The horses were fed ____.”",["oats","oat's","oat"],"oats","The grain used as feed is conventionally called oats.","plural"),Q("oats.q4","oats.s1","meaning","Oats belong to which broad food group?",["cereal grains","citrus fruits","shellfish"],"cereal grains","Oats are a grain crop, unlike fruit or seafood.","meaning")]});
  D("obedience",{etymology:E("From Old French obedience and Latin oboedientia, from oboedire ‘obey, listen to’; the Latin verb combines ob- with audire ‘hear’.",null,"Latin oboedientia < oboedire < ob + audire",null,"Etymonline, obedience (https://www.etymonline.com/word/obedience)."),contexts:[C("obedience.s1","通用","The puppy learned obedience by responding calmly when its trainer called.","小狗在訓練員呼喚時平靜地回應，逐漸學會了服從。","Obedience names the state or practice of doing what an authority asks.","Uncountable noun after learned; by introduces the method.","Responding to the trainer’s instruction demonstrates compliance with a person."),C("obedience.s2","法律","The bridge must be built in obedience to the new safety regulations.","這座橋必須依照新的安全規定建造。","In obedience to means in strict accordance with rules or orders.","The fixed prepositional phrase in obedience to is followed by a noun phrase.","The regulations are rules being followed, selecting the rule-compliance sense.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","The bridge was inspected in obedience with the safety code.","The bridge was inspected in obedience to the safety code.","The established phrase is in obedience to, not in obedience with.")],quiz:[Q("obedience.q1","obedience.s1","meaning","A dog shows obedience when it ___.",["follows its handler’s command","hides from every person","barks without stopping"],"follows its handler’s command","Obedience is doing what a person in authority tells you to do.","meaning"),Q("obedience.q2","obedience.s2","collocation","Complete the phrase: “The work was done in obedience ____ the order.”",["to","with","at"],"to","The standard collocation is in obedience to an order or rule.","collocation"),Q("obedience.q3","obedience.s2","context","Which sentence shows obedience to a rule?",["The crew followed the evacuation protocol.","The crew ignored the posted evacuation protocol.","The crew invented a new protocol but did not use it."],"The crew followed the evacuation protocol.","Following the protocol is compliance with an established rule.","context"),Q("obedience.q4","obedience.s1","meaning","A teacher praises a class for obedience. What is being praised?",["their willingness to follow instructions","their ability to write quickly","their refusal to listen"],"their willingness to follow instructions","The general sense is compliance with instructions from an authority.","meaning")]});
  D("obedient",{etymology:E("From Old French obedient and Latin oboedientem, the present participle of oboedire ‘listen to, obey’; it shares a root with obedience.",null,"Latin oboedientem < oboedire",null,"Etymonline, obedient (https://www.etymonline.com/word/obedient)."),contexts:[C("obedient.s1","通用","The obedient dog waited at the gate until its owner gave the signal.","這隻聽話的狗在門口等著，直到主人發出信號。","Obedient describes an animal that follows a command or instruction.","Attributive adjective before dog; until introduces the limit of waiting.","Waiting for the owner’s signal shows compliance with an instruction."),C("obedient.s2","家庭","Her parents described her as an obedient child who always treated them respectfully.","她的父母說她是個孝順聽話的孩子，總是尊敬他們。","The child sense combines good behavior with respect toward parents.","As + adjective + noun complement; who clause adds characteristic behavior.","The explicit parental respect selects the narrower child-related sense.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The obedient pupil followed every classroom instruction and refused to do what the teacher said.","The obedient pupil followed every classroom instruction the teacher gave.","Obedient means following instructions, so refusing them contradicts the adjective.")],quiz:[Q("obedient.q1","obedient.s1","meaning","An obedient dog is most likely to ___.",["sit when its handler gives the command","run away whenever called","ignore every signal"],"sit when its handler gives the command","The adjective means doing what an order or rule says.","meaning"),Q("obedient.q2","obedient.s2","meaning","An obedient child in the family sense is described as ___.",["well-behaved and respectful to parents","unable to learn anything","always disobedient at home"],"well-behaved and respectful to parents","The narrower source sense highlights good behavior and respect for parents.","meaning"),Q("obedient.q3","obedient.s1","context","Which sentence uses obedient for compliance with an instruction?",["The obedient horse stopped at the rider’s signal.","The obedient horse broke the fence and ran off.","The horse was obediently beautiful."],"The obedient horse stopped at the rider’s signal.","Stopping at the signal demonstrates the animal follows directions.","context"),Q("obedient.q4","obedient.s2","word-choice","Her parents called her ____ because she was respectful and well behaved.",["obedient","obedience","obediently"],"obedient","The blank after called her needs an adjective describing the child.","word-choice")]});
  D("obese",{etymology:E("From Latin obesus ‘having eaten oneself fat’, past participle of obedere ‘eat away’; the word is now a clinical adjective concerning excess body fat and health.",null,"Latin obesus < obedere",null,"Etymonline, obese (https://www.etymonline.com/word/obese)."),contexts:[C("obese.s1","医学","The physician diagnosed the patient as obese after assessing health risks related to excess body fat.","醫師在評估與過多體脂相關的健康風險後，診斷患者為肥胖。","Obese is the clinical adjective describing excess body fat that may harm health.","Obese follows diagnosed as and describes the patient’s medical status.","The health risk and physician setting make this the medical sense, not a casual comment on appearance.")],mistakes:[M("register","The clinic called the patient obese as a joke about her lunch order.","The clinic assessed the patient’s health using a clinical measure of obesity.","Obese is a sensitive clinical descriptor and should not be used as a joke or inferred from one meal.")],quiz:[Q("obese.q1","obese.s1","meaning","In clinical use, obese describes someone with ___.",["excess body fat that may harm health","a temporary dislike of vegetables","a very tall body with no health concern"],"excess body fat that may harm health","The source defines a medical state involving excess fat and likely health effects.","meaning"),Q("obese.q2","obese.s1","register","Which use is most appropriate?",["A clinician discusses an obesity diagnosis respectfully.","A stranger mocks someone’s body at lunch.","A menu uses the word to guess a customer’s health."],"A clinician discusses an obesity diagnosis respectfully.","The word belongs in careful health-related discussion, not ridicule or unsupported guesses.","register"),Q("obese.q3","obese.s1","context","Which detail signals the medical sense?",["A doctor assesses health risks linked to excess body fat.","A fashion review comments on a coat’s cut.","A child picks a larger serving."],"A doctor assesses health risks linked to excess body fat.","A medical assessment of associated health risk matches the clinical adjective.","context"),Q("obese.q4","obese.s1","word-choice","A respectful medical report should use ____ only when clinically supported.",["obese","obesely","obesity"],"obese","The sentence needs an adjective, and this sensitive clinical term requires evidence.","word-choice")]});
  D("obesity",{etymology:E("From Latin obesitas, from obesus ‘fat’; obesus is related to obedere, literally ‘eat away’. Modern medical usage treats obesity as a health condition rather than a moral judgment.",null,"Latin obesitas < obesus",null,"Etymonline, obese (https://www.etymonline.com/word/obese); WHO, Obesity and overweight (https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/obesity-and-overweight)."),contexts:[C("obesity.s1","医学","The clinician explained that obesity is a complex health condition influenced by many factors.","臨床醫師解釋，肥胖是一種受多種因素影響的複雜健康狀況。","Obesity names the medical condition of excess body fat that may affect health.","Uncountable singular noun as the subject; that clause characterizes the condition.","The clinical framing treats obesity as a condition, not as a personal failing."),C("obesity.s2","公共卫生","The report tracks obesity across regions to plan prevention services for the whole population.","報告追蹤各地的肥胖問題，以便為整個人口規劃預防服務。","Obesity can refer to widespread excess weight as a population-level public health problem.","Tracks takes a broad issue as object; across regions signals population comparison.","The regional surveillance and population planning select the public-health pattern sense.")],mistakes:[M("register","The article claimed obesity is simply a moral failure rather than a health condition.","The article described obesity as a complex health condition, not a moral failure.","Obesity is a health condition influenced by multiple factors; labeling it only a moral failure is inaccurate and stigmatizing.")],quiz:[Q("obesity.q1","obesity.s1","meaning","In a clinical note, obesity is treated as ___.",["a health condition involving excess body fat","a synonym for hunger","a brief mood"],"a health condition involving excess body fat","The medical sense concerns excess body fat with potential health effects.","meaning"),Q("obesity.q2","obesity.s2","meaning","A report comparing obesity rates by region studies ___.",["a population-level public health pattern","one person’s breakfast","the price of gym shoes"],"a population-level public health pattern","Regional rates concern prevalence across a population.","meaning"),Q("obesity.q3","obesity.s2","context","Which project examines obesity as a public-health issue?",["A survey compares rates across age groups and districts.","A doctor weighs one patient during an appointment.","A cook tests a soup recipe."],"A survey compares rates across age groups and districts.","Comparing rates across groups is population-level surveillance.","context"),Q("obesity.q4","obesity.s1","register","Which sentence is the most responsible clinical wording?",["Obesity is a complex condition with biological and social influences.","Obesity proves that people are lazy.","Obesity is a joke about someone’s body."],"Obesity is a complex condition with biological and social influences.","This wording describes a condition without stigmatizing people or asserting a simplistic cause.","register")]});
  D("obey",{etymology:E("From Old French obeir and Latin oboedire ‘listen to, obey’, literally ob- ‘toward’ + audire ‘hear’; the verb developed from listening to compliance.","ob-","audire","-ire","Etymonline, obey (https://www.etymonline.com/word/obey)."),contexts:[C("obey.s1","通用","The child obeyed her coach and stopped before crossing the track.","孩子聽從教練的指示，在穿越跑道前停了下來。","Obey means do what a person in authority tells you.","Transitive verb with coach as object; and coordinates the command’s action.","The coach gives an instruction that the child follows."),C("obey.s2","法律","Drivers must obey the posted speed limit even when the road looks empty.","即使道路看起來空曠，駕駛人也必須遵守張貼的限速。","Obey means act according to a law or rule.","Must + bare verb; the posted limit is the rule object.","A speed limit is a formal rule rather than a person’s direct command.")],mistakes:[M("collocation","Motorists must obey to the posted speed limit.","Motorists must obey the posted speed limit.","Obey takes a direct object without to; ‘comply with’ is the alternative construction.")],quiz:[Q("obey.q1","obey.s1","meaning","If a child obeys the coach, the child ___.",["does what the coach says","argues about every rule","leaves without listening"],"does what the coach says","The person sense is to follow an instruction from someone in authority.","meaning"),Q("obey.q2","obey.s2","grammar","Choose the standard construction.",["obey the law","obey to the law","obey with the law"],"obey the law","Obey is transitive and takes the rule directly as its object.","grammar"),Q("obey.q3","obey.s2","context","Which sentence uses obey for a rule?",["Cyclists obey the traffic signal.","Mira obeyed her piano teacher’s request.","The dog obeyed its owner’s call."],"Cyclists obey the traffic signal.","A traffic signal is a rule or instruction governing road use.","context"),Q("obey.q4","obey.s1","word-choice","The guard asked visitors to ____ the evacuation order.",["obey","obedient","obedience"],"obey","The sentence needs a bare verb after to; obey means follow an order.","word-choice")]});
